@startuml
title Adaptive per-face vertex displacement clamp (replaces flat 0.8 constant)

start

:for every mesh vertex, compute its RAW radical-center\nposition from its 3 owning faces' weights - NO clamp applied yet;

partition "per-face validity check (every face, every round)" {
  :build this face's own hexagon from its 6 corners'\nRAW candidate positions;
  if (is this hexagon simple - no two of its own\nnon-adjacent edges cross?) then (yes)
    :this face needs no correction this round;
  else (no)
    :binary-search the largest shrink factor t in [0,1]\nsuch that scaling every one of THIS face's 6 corners\nt of the way from its original position toward its\nraw candidate keeps the hexagon simple;
    note right
      why binary search, not a formula: simplicity is a
      yes/no geometric test (segment-intersection over
      the 6 edges), not a smooth function - there's no
      closed form for "how far is too far" once more
      than one corner has moved. Assumes simplicity is
      monotonic in t (true near t=0, breaks past some
      threshold, never flips back) - verified directly
      by a property test scanning t densely on synthetic
      cases, not just assumed.
    end note
    :record "face X requires vertex V's own scale <= t"\nfor each of this face's 6 corners;
  endif
}

partition "reconcile shared vertices (every vertex is owned by up to 3 faces)" {
  :for each vertex, take the SMALLEST scale required by\nany of its owning faces (most conservative wins) -\ndefault to 1.0 (no scaling) if no owning face required one;
  note right
    a vertex can never move a different amount for two
    faces that share it - that would reopen the exact
    seam gap the hex-mesh design exists to close. One
    scale, one final position, read identically by every
    face touching that vertex - same watertightness
    guarantee EdgeDisplacement already relies on.
  end note
  :apply that one scale to get this vertex's FINAL\ndisplaced position;
}

:every face's hexagon, built from these final positions,\nis now simple BY CONSTRUCTION - not because a magic\nconstant happened to be small enough on the seeds tested;

stop
@enduml
